# Project Context Ledger (.agent)

Last updated: 2026-08-27 (Admin: removed footer JTech credit + theme customizer gear)
Repository: C:\Users\Hp\Documents\personal\event management
Default branch: main

## Purpose
This file is the persistent project context for AI-assisted chats.
It is the single source of truth for:
- current architecture and module inventory
- **mandatory** backend/frontend feature patterns (copy these, do not invent new ones)
- important conventions
- active runtime/dev state
- recent changes and reasoning

Every meaningful change to the codebase must also update this file.
**Other chats should be able to read only this file and correctly scaffold a new feature.**

## Current Runtime / Workspace State
- Full-stack Laravel + React SPA (Blade shell + Vite React app)
- Dev: `composer run dev` (Unix) or `composer run dev:windows` (Windows)
  - Laravel serve: `http://localhost:8001` (`composer run dev` and `composer run dev:windows`)
  - Vite HMR via `npm run dev` / pnpm Vite (still **5173**)
  - Queue worker: `php artisan queue:listen`
  - Scheduler: `php artisan schedule:work` (or cron) for `ExpirePendingPayments` + `ExpireOrganizerSubscriptions` every 5 min
- API base URL (axios): `/api/v1` (same-origin)
- Absolute API examples: `http://localhost:8001/api/v1`
- Local `APP_URL` should be `http://localhost:8001` (`.env` / `.env.example`)
- Health: `GET /up`; API ping: `GET /api/ping`
- Seed admin: `admin@example.com` / `password` (`user_type=admin`, role `admin`, all permissions)
- DB: MySQL `eventdb` (local); tests use SQLite `:memory:`
- Known gotchas:
  - Windows `dev:windows` and Unix `dev` serve Admin Laravel on port **8001** (Vite stays on **5173**)
  - Sanctum stateful defaults include `localhost:8001` / `127.0.0.1:8001`
  - **API client auth (Prompt 3b, simplified 2026-08-18):** All `/api/*` routes require `X-API-Key` (`verify.api.client` / `VerifyApiClientSignature` on `routes/api.php`). Lookup: `api_clients` where `public_key` matches and `active = true`. Errors: `missing_api_key` (header absent/empty), `invalid_api_key` (unknown or inactive). **No** `X-API-Timestamp` / `X-API-Signature` — HMAC was removed because the Web App is a Vite SPA with no server to hide `WEBAPP_API_SECRET`. `api_clients.secret` column remains in DB unused by verification. Admin SPA axios sends `X-API-Key` from `VITE_WEBAPP_API_PUBLIC_KEY`. Web App sends the same public key. Rotate by updating env `WEBAPP_API_PUBLIC_KEY` + `php artisan db:seed --class=ApiClientSeeder`.
  - **Public API-key-only catalog (Web App, no Bearer):** `GET /api/v1/events`, `GET /api/v1/events/{id}`, `GET /api/v1/event-categories`, `GET /api/v1/events/{id}/form-fields`, **`GET /api/v1/platform/branding`**. `X-API-Key` still required. No `auth:sanctum` / `admin.panel`. Without an `admin-panel` Bearer, events are filtered to `published|registration_open|sold_out|registration_closed|ongoing` (`Event::scopePublicCatalog` / `EventStatus::publicCatalogValues()`). Draft, cancelled, and completed are omitted; public show of those returns **404**. Admin-panel Bearer (Admin SPA) still returns **all** statuses including draft/cancelled. Public payloads hide organizer `email` / `phone` / `contact_name` (only `id` + `business_name`) and do not load `discountCodes`. Public show eager-loads ticket types, speakers, sponsors, sessions, category, images. **Form-fields** (`PublicEventFormFieldController`): public callers get **active** fields only; admin-panel Bearer + `view event form fields` still gets the full admin payload (inactive included). **Platform branding** (`PlatformBrandingController`): returns `{ name, logo_url, logo_dark_url, icon_url }` only (nulls when no org row); never email/phone/address. Managed in Admin Settings → Organization. All other Admin event/category routes remain API-key + Sanctum + `admin.panel` + permissions.
  - **Web App HTTP surface (Prompt 0):** explicit `/api/v1/participant/*` (`participant.web`) and `/api/v1/organizer/*` (`organizer.web`). Do **not** reuse Admin routes for Web tokens. Admin SPA routes/permissions unchanged. Domain services reused (ParticipationService, PaymentService, EventStatusMachine, EventQuota, QrValidationService, etc.).
  - **Vite must be running** for Admin SPA (`@vite` in `app.blade.php`). If Vite dies, Laravel throws `ViteManifestNotFoundException` (`public/build/manifest.json` missing — we do not commit a production build). Symptom: Internal Server Error on `http://localhost:8001`. Fix: restart `composer run dev:windows` (or `npm run dev`). Cause seen: `.env` change restarts Vite, then `laravel-vite-plugin@1.3.0` crashes (`Cannot read properties of null (reading 'family')`). Mitigated in `vite.config.js`: `server.host=127.0.0.1`, ignore `**/.env`.
  - Lockfile is **pnpm** (`pnpm-lock.yaml`); npm also works
  - Queue/cache/session default to **database** — migrate before first run
  - Organizations logo columns: create migration includes `logo_dark_url`/`icon_url`; alter is `2025_08_24_090000_...` (never `2025_01_27_...` before create)
  - Do not commit `.env` or secrets
  - Organization is effectively **single-tenant profile** (not a full CRUD list page like Users)
  - After permission changes: reseed `RolePermissionSeeder` (or sync admin role) so gates match routes
  - Full suite: **252 passed**, **3 pre-existing `ExceptionHandlerTest` failures** (SPA catch-all) — only acceptable failures
  - Run `php artisan migrate` for package duration/tier + `organizer_subscription_orders` + subscription snapshots (Prompt 15)
  - Seed: `InvitationSystemTemplateSeeder` (4 placeholder designs) via DatabaseSeeder
  - **No demo/dummy catalog seeder.** `DemoDataSeeder` was removed. Fresh `db:seed` only boots roles/permissions (+ admin user), API client, settings, event categories, and invitation system templates. Create organizers/events/packages via Admin or Web App.
  - After Prompt 13/14/15 permissions: reseed `RolePermissionSeeder` when needed (`view/manage invitation templates` already exist)
  - **FormCombobox / pickers:** Headless UI calls `displayValue(null)` when nothing is selected — formatters and `FormCombobox` must treat null as `""`. Avoid Unicode middle-dot (`·`) in template literals on Windows/Vite Babel (use ASCII ` - ` instead).
  - **Ownership (Prompt 13):** Admin = platform owner; Organizer = event owner. Event-operation actions (manual pay, QR check-in, Waafi charge) reject `admin-panel` tokens with `403` + `error_code: action_requires_organizer_scope` via `RejectsAdminPanelOrganizerActions`.
  - **Event hub is a full page** (`/events/:id`) with lazy-loaded tabs for all event-scoped sub-resources (tickets, participants, payments+refunds, gallery upload, invitation preview, add-ons, analytics, finance). List row-click navigates; do not reopen this hub in a side panel.
  - **Invitation designer / generation / overlay editor = Web App Phase 2** — Admin only manages system template library + read-only event preview.

## Flagged Decisions (CLIENT REVIEW — confirm before Web App pack)
These were decided during Admin Prompts 1–12. Confirm or correct before Web App work:

1. **Refund after payout recorded** — Block refund when it would leave collected funds &lt; reserved/paid-out payouts. API: `errors.error_code: ["refund_blocked_payout_recorded"]`. No automatic clawback. **Admin refund UI built (Prompt 14)** on Event Detail Payments panel (`refund payments`).
2. **Payout scope** — **Per-event** payout requests only (not multi-event / organizer-wide batches).
3. **Admin edit rights on organizer identity** — **Confirmed / implemented:** Admins PATCH `business_name`, `contact_name`, `email`, `phone` (`edit organizers`). Password remains Web App / self-service. Status via suspend/reactivate.
4. **Share Event (spec 12.3 MUST)** — **Explicitly deferred to Web App pack** (share-link generation is front-end). Not implemented in Admin.
5. **Currency** — Platform assumes **USD** for WaafiPay / payments / payouts.
6. **Pending payment stuck path** — After 15 minutes: payment → `failed`, participation → `cancelled`, ticket quantity released (`ExpirePendingPayments`).
7. **WaafiPay success rule** — Both `responseCode === "2001"` **and** `state === "approved"` (case-insensitive). Timeout **180s**.
8. **Commission** — Snapshotted on payout request create; changing Settings rate does **not** rewrite existing requests.
9. **Event `monetized`** — Derived from paid ticket types; cannot be forced false while paid tiers exist.
10. **Capacity → `sold_out`** — Sync when capacity is exhausted; `null` capacity = unlimited (distinct from `0`).
11. **Organizer email uniqueness** — Unique on `organizers.email` only; may equal a `users.email` (separate identities).
12. **Suspension cascade** — Suspending an organizer does **not** delete events; events stay admin-visible; organizer Web edits blocked while suspended.
13. **Soft-delete FK policy** — Future `organizer_id` FKs use **`restrictOnDelete`**; soft-delete preserves rows for relations.
14. **Form field delete** — If answers exist → deactivate (`active=false`); else hard-delete. Historical answers never retroactively invalidated. **Key cannot change on update.**
15. **QR outcomes** — Three results: `valid` | `already_used` | `invalid`. Cancelled/refunded → `invalid` **before** `already_used`. Re-scan logs `already_used` without double check-in.
16. **Packages delete/archive** — Blocked if any subscription history exists (active or cancelled).
17. **Ticket type force-delete** — Blocked when `quantity_sold > 0`; soft-delete still allowed.
18. **Cancelled events** — Cannot be force-deleted.
19. **Admin Users `user_type`** — Read-only in Admin UI; creates force `admin`; updates ignore `user_type`.
20. **Orphaned permission cleanup (Prompt 11)** — Removed unused seeder permission `view reports`. Dashboard uses `view dashboard`. Logs routes re-gated with `view logs`.
21. **Prompt 12 Admin write expansion** — Platform admins have write/override on ticket types, discount codes, form fields, announcements, sponsors/speakers/sessions, and participation add/cancel-with-reason. **Manual cash payment was removed from Admin in Prompt 13** (organizer-scoped).
22. **Manual payments** — Service `PaymentService::recordManual` kept for Web App. `POST /payments/manual` **rejects admin-panel tokens** (`action_requires_organizer_scope`). Historical activity logs retained.
23. **Full Event create UI** — Still moderation-focused in Admin (no full organizer-style create form). API `POST /events` exists; gallery upload API exists but FE remains delete-focused. **BY DESIGN** unless product asks for admin create.
24. **Ownership boundary (Prompt 13 / Prompt 0)** — Admin = platform owner; Organizer = event owner. QR scanner UI and Waafi charge UI were **never built** in Admin. Admin `POST /qr-scan-logs/validate` and `POST /payments/charge` remain scope-blocked for admin-panel tokens. **Web API now exists:** participant charge, organizer QR validate, organizer invitation designer endpoints. Invitation PDF compositing and Share Event remain deferred.
25. **Certificate re-issue (Prompt 13)** — Admin can force re-issue via `POST /certificates/{participation_id}/reissue` (`reissue certificates`). Requires `checked_in`; fails safely without deleting old row on generation error.
26. **Feedback moderation (Prompt 13)** — Platform-wide `/feedback` list + hide/show (`event_feedback.hidden`). Soft-hide only. **Web App MUST filter `where hidden = false`** on any public/organizer feedback query.
27. **Invitation preview (Prompt 13/14)** — Read-only `InvitationTemplatePreview` on Event Detail; uses `GET /events/{id}/invitation-template` + `eventApi.getInvitationTemplate`.
28. **Prompt 14 UI completeness** — Platform `/payments`, `/certificates`, `/subscriptions`; Event Detail payments+refunds + gallery upload. **Item 7 (rebuild Feedback) skipped** — Feedback already complete from Prompt 13; do not regress.
29. **Invitation system (Prompt 15)** — Platform library `invitation_system_templates` (Admin CRUD under Settings). Event configs support `mode=template|custom`. Designer/generation/compositing = **Web App Phase 2**. Canvas locked at **800×1100px portrait**.
30. **Public event catalog (Web App)** — `GET /events`, `GET /events/{id}`, `GET /event-categories` are API-key-only (no participant Bearer). Public statuses: `published`, `registration_open`, `sold_out`, `registration_closed`, `ongoing`. Admin-panel Bearer keeps full unfiltered Admin list/detail.
