## Tech Stack
### Backend
- PHP 8.2+, Laravel 12
- Auth: Laravel Sanctum (Bearer tokens)
- RBAC: spatie/laravel-permission (`permission:` / `role:` middleware aliases in `bootstrap/app.php`)
- Audit: spatie/laravel-activitylog (via `BaseController::logActivity` or explicit `activity()` for Settings)
- Location: stevebauman/location
- Queue: `SendEmailJob`, `MailService`, **`ExpirePendingPayments`** (scheduled every 5 min). Default queue connection: **`database`** (`QUEUE_CONNECTION`); `composer run dev` / `dev:windows` starts `php artisan queue:listen`.
- **Payments (Phase 6):** WaafiPay Hormuud EVC via `WaafiPayService` → `POST {WAAFI_BASE_URL}` (default `https://api.waafipay.net/asm`), credentials in `config/waafipay.php` / `.env` (`WAAFI_MERCHANT_UID`, `WAAFI_API_USER_ID`, `WAAFI_API_KEY`). **HTTP timeout 180s**. Currency **USD**. Never log `apiKey`. Tests mock HTTP.
  - **Waafi failure-message pipeline:** `WaafiPayService::interpretResponse()` first checks HTTP status — **HTTP 401 returns `failure_code: gateway_auth_error`** (`"Payment service configuration error. Please contact support."`) before JSON decode. For HTTP 200 business declines: `extractFailureReason(array $body)` derives `failure_reason` using priority: **(1) `params.description`** (Waafi human-readable field, Somali or English, verbatim) → **(2) mapped English phrase** when `responseMsg` is a known technical code (see `ERROR_FALLBACK_REASON`) → **(3) `responseMsg` itself** when non-empty and not a pure `UPPERCASE_IDENTIFIER` → **(4) stable fallback `"Payment was not approved."`**. `failure_code` from `resolveFailureCode($responseMsg)` using `ERROR_CODE_MAP`. `sanitizeCustomerMessage()` strips `"Error: "`-style prefixes and rejects identifiers. Never translates; never exposes credentials/stack traces.
  - **Real production root-cause (2026-08-19):** All real Waafi calls returned **HTTP 401** — API credentials not configured/invalid in `.env` (`WAAFI_MERCHANT_UID`, `WAAFI_API_USER_ID`, `WAAFI_API_KEY`). Waafi 401 response has null/empty body so all previous extraction fallback reached `"Payment was not approved."` instead of surfacing the auth problem. Fixed by HTTP status check before body inspection.
  - **Participant payment API (`POST /api/v1/participant/payments/charge`):** response explicitly serializes `failure_code` + `failure_reason` via `serializePayment()` in `ParticipantPaymentController`. Business declines: HTTP 200 + `data.status=failed` + populated failure fields. Server/transport errors: HTTP 502.

### Frontend
- React 18 + TypeScript, Vite 5, `laravel-vite-plugin`
- Redux Toolkit + TanStack React Query
- React Router DOM 6 (`resources/js/src/router/routes.tsx`)
- UI: Tailwind 3, MUI, Mantine, Headless UI; shared `DataTableWithSidebar`, `GenericModal`
- Forms: React Hook Form / Formik; Yup / Zod
- i18n: i18next (`public/locales/{en,ae}/translation.json`)
- HTTP: `resources/js/src/utils/axios.ts` → `baseURL: "/api/v1"`
- Nav: `resources/js/src/lib/sidebar.ts` (permission-filtered)

### Build / Tooling
- Composer + pnpm/npm
- PHPUnit (`composer test`), Laravel Pint, Vite
- Agent enforcement: `check-agent-update.sh`, `install-agent-hook.ps1`, `.github/workflows/agent-context-check.yml`

## Run Commands
- Install: `composer install`; `pnpm install` (or `npm install`)
- Env: `.env.example` → `.env`; `php artisan key:generate`; DB config; `php artisan migrate`; `php artisan db:seed`
- Primary dev: `composer run dev` / `composer run dev:windows`
- Tests: `composer test` / `php artisan test`
- Hook once: `powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File .\install-agent-hook.ps1`

