**Explicitly deferred:** Share Event → Web App pack. Organizer door scanner / Waafi charge UI / invitation designer / feedback submit UX → Web App.
**Removed from Admin (Prompt 13):** manual mark-as-paid UI; admin use of QR validate & payment charge (scope-blocked). QR scanner screen and payment charging screen were **never built** in Admin FE.

## Backend Structure Notes
- Controllers live in `app/Http/Controllers/Api/` and extend `BaseController` except `SettingsController` (uses `activity()` directly).
- Models in `app/Models/`; enums in `app/Enums/`; domain services in `app/Services/`.
- Jobs: `ExpirePendingPayments`; Events/Listeners: `ParticipationCheckedIn` → `IssueAttendanceCertificate`.
- Route files under `routes/api/v1/` imported from `routes/api.php`.
- Factories under `database/factories/` for all major models used in tests.
- Seeders: `RolePermissionSeeder`, `ApiClientSeeder`, `SettingsSeeder`, `EventCategorySeeder`, `InvitationSystemTemplateSeeder`. **No** `DemoDataSeeder` (removed).

## Frontend Structure Notes
- Entry: `main.tsx`, `App.tsx`
- Router: `router/routes.tsx`, `router/index.tsx` (lazy + `permissions`)
- Sidebar: `lib/sidebar.ts` + `filterMenuByPermissions` / `cleanEmptySections`
- Shared list UX: `DataTableWithSidebar` (sidebar optional), `StatusFilterBar`, `DetailPageHeader`, `DetailTabs`, `GenericModal`, `GenericSidebar`, `DetailSidebar`
- Nested Event hub lists: `SimpleAdminTable` (`components/SimpleAdminTable.tsx`) — compact `<table>` matching list-page look (headers, `text-sm`, badges, action buttons). Do **not** stack bordered cards/`<ul>` for ticket types, discounts, registrations, payments, form fields, speakers, sessions, sponsors, announcements, gallery, or certificates-on-event. Overview/Analytics use `EventMetricCard`. Invitation tab: thumbnail + `EventField` customizations (color swatches) + overlay positions table (never raw `x=, y=` strings).
- Amount helper: `utils/money.ts` `formatMoney` → `"15.00 USD"`
- Column extras: `hideBelow`, `minWidth` on `ColumnConfig`
- Hooks: `useSidebarDetail`, `useConfirmDialog`, `usePermission`, `useAuth`, `useAuthInit`
- Store: `authSlice`, `organizationSlice`, `themeConfigSlice`
- Axios Bearer from storage/Redux + **`X-API-Key`** (`utils/axios.ts`; env `VITE_WEBAPP_API_PUBLIC_KEY`). HMAC signing was removed (Vite SPA cannot hide a secret). Web App should send the same `X-API-Key` plus `web-participant` or `organizer-web` Bearer on `/participant/*` and `/organizer/*`.

## Data + Domain Conventions

### MySQL ENUM for statuses (2026-08-20)
Domain status / constrained-choice columns are native MySQL `ENUM` (not free-text VARCHAR). Helper: `App\Support\EnumColumn::modify`. Migration: `2026_08_20_153000_convert_status_columns_to_mysql_enums.php`. App layer still uses PHP backed enums + Eloquent casts. SQLite tests leave strings (EnumColumn no-op). Do not invent new status strings — extend the PHP enum **and** a follow-up `ALTER … ENUM(...)` migration together. `settings.status` remains boolean.

### Soft deletes & trash
| Resource | SoftDeletes | Admin Trash tab |
|----------|-------------|-----------------|
| Users | yes | yes |
| Roles | yes | yes |
| Organizers | yes | yes |
| Events | yes | yes |
| Event categories | yes | yes |
| Ticket types | yes | no (Event hub Ticket Types tab / force rules) |
| Discount codes | yes | no (Event hub Ticket Types tab soft-delete) |
| Organizations | yes | no (single profile) |
| Packages / payments / payouts / participations / add-ons | no soft-delete trash UI | — |

### Auth & identity
- **Machine clients (Prompt 3b):** `api_clients` table + `VerifyApiClientSignature` middleware on all `/api/*`. Verification is **`X-API-Key` only** (active `public_key` lookup). `api_clients.secret` is unused by middleware (column kept). Seeded from `WEBAPP_API_PUBLIC_KEY`. Admin Settings → **API Clients** read-only list (`view api clients`).
- **Public vs authenticated API:** `X-API-Key` is always required. Bearer (`admin-panel`) is required for Admin writes and most reads. **Exceptions (API-key-only, no Bearer):** `GET /api/v1/events`, `GET /api/v1/events/{id}`, `GET /api/v1/event-categories`, `GET /api/v1/events/{id}/form-fields`. Participant `web-participant` tokens do **not** unlock drafts — treated as public catalog. Web participant/organizer surfaces use dedicated groups (see Web API surface).
- `User.user_type`: `admin` | `user`. Admin UI type is **read-only**. Admin creates force `admin`. An admin user **with a web-participant token** may use `/participant/*`.
- Organizers are **not** Users — separate table, Sanctum ability `organizer-web`, email unique only on organizers table. Admin may **edit** identity (`edit organizers` / PATCH). Organizer self-service: `PATCH /organizer-auth/profile` + `POST /organizer-auth/change-password` (current password required).
- Spatie permissions gate Admin Panel; FE mirrors with route + sidebar `permissions`.

### Events & registration
- Status transitions only via `EventStatusMachine` / `POST …/transition` — never free-text PATCH status.
- **Public catalog filter:** `EventStatus::publicCatalogValues()` = `published`, `registration_open`, `sold_out`, `registration_closed`, `ongoing`. Applied in `EventController::index` / `show` unless the caller has an `admin-panel` Sanctum token. Completed is **not** public.
- Public event JSON: organizer visible fields `id`, `business_name` only; no discount codes; show includes ticket types, speakers, sponsors, sessions, category, images, **`event_mode`**, **`online_url`**, **`why_attend`**, **`banner_path`**, **`banner_url`**.
- Organizer create: `event_mode` required (`in_person` / `online` / `hybrid`). `online_url` required for `online` and `hybrid`. City/address/lat/lng stay optional except lat/lng pair rule. Online-only must not send fake venue.
- **`why_attend`:** nullable JSON string array (max 6, each max 200 after trim; empty strings dropped). Null/empty → Web App hides the section.
- **VIP classification:** `ticket_types.is_vip` boolean (default `false`). Never infer VIP from `name`. Admin + organizer create/update accept `is_vip`; public/organizer/admin ticket JSON includes it. Admin Event hub Ticket Types tab shows VIP badge + form switch. Factory default `false`; state `vip()`.
- **Banner contract:** stored `banner_path` is typically `/assets/images/events/{file}` under **`public/`** (same folder as gallery; **not** `/storage/...`). Absolute `http(s)` URLs (demo picsum) pass through. Appended `banner_url` is `url('/'+path)` for relative paths. Organizer upload: `POST /organizer/events/{event}/banner` field **`banner`**. String `banner_path` still accepted on create/update. If the Web App prefixes `/storage/`, that is a frontend `getMediaUrl()` bug — Laravel is correct.
- Registration gates (capacity + deadline) are independent (`EventRegistrationGate`).
- `monetized` derived from paid ticket types.
- Participations: waitlist when full; join/promote/cancel in DB transaction with atomic ticket claim/release.
- Form answers validated at submit only; no FK from answers → schema rows.
- QR token issued for confirmed (paid/free) participations; validation order: not found → cancelled → refunded → already_used → not claimable → valid.

### Money
- `payments` is SoT; participation `payment_status` is mirror.
- Currency USD; WaafiPay both-conditions success; pending expire 15 min. Charge amount is `DiscountPricingService::chargeAmountFor` (participation snapshot `final_amount` if set, else ticket price). Client cannot override amount.
- Payouts **per event**; commission snapshotted at request; double-payout guarded with `lockForUpdate`.
- Refund blocked when outstanding would go negative (`refund_blocked_payout_recorded`).
- **Manual payments:** `gateway=manual`, completed immediately, `POST /payments/manual`, QR token issued when paid.

### Searchable FK pickers
- All admin forms/filters that need a related entity use `FormCombobox` + `useEntitySearch` (see Scaffold §D). Never raw ID number inputs.
- `formatEventOption` / `formatUserOption` and `FormCombobox` must accept **null** (Headless UI clears selection). Label separators: ASCII ` - ` (not Unicode `·`).

### API / FE patterns
- List responses are Laravel paginator-shaped (`IApiResponse<T>`); filters `filter[field]=value`.
- Mutations use React Query; invalidate table keys after success.
- Single organization profile for branding.
- Compact tables + dense details (see UI rules below).
- Activity log on all Admin write paths.

## Known Risks / Watchouts
- Full suite: **199 passed / 3 failed** — only `ExceptionHandlerTest` (pre-existing SPA catch-all).
- **Public catalog vs Admin list:** API-key-only `GET /events` hides draft/cancelled/completed. Admin SPA must keep sending `admin-panel` Bearer or the Events table will look empty of drafts.
- **Refund-after-payout** and Share Event still need client awareness; refund UI not built.
- **WaafiPay:** never call production from CI; mock HTTP; never log apiKey; production PHP/web timeout must allow 180s.
- Run scheduler so `ExpirePendingPayments` runs; queue worker for announcement emails.
- Reseed permissions after migrate when gates change (Prompt 12 added manage announcements/sponsors/speakers/sessions + edit/delete discount codes).
- After migrate: seed permissions + `EventCategorySeeder`; migrate `payments.gateway`.
- Participation ticket lock + payment refund/release must stay transactional — regressions in `ParticipationModuleTest` + `PaymentPayoutModuleTest` + `Prompt12CategoryATest`.

## Agent Behavior Rules (for every chat)
1. Read this `.agent` file first.
2. Before coding a feature, inspect the closest existing twin (Users or Roles) and copy its structure.
3. Controllers extend `BaseController`; FE services extend `BaseApi`; pages use `index` + `components/{Detail,Form,Modal}` unless the domain is an documented exception.
4. New API routes go in `routes/api/v1/<name>.php` and are imported from `routes/api.php`.
5. Add/update TypeScript types and re-export from `types/index.ts`.
6. **UI must stay consistent, modern, and compact** — follow `.cursor/rules/ui-consistency-compact-data.mdc`:
   - Reuse theme components (`panel`, `btn`, forms, `DataTableWithSidebar`, `StatusFilterBar`, `GenericModal`, etc.)
   - Tables = important scannable fields only; no truncated headers; amounts via `formatMoney`
   - Details = complete useful fields; **side panel vs full page** by data volume (see UI conventions)
   - Status filters = `StatusFilterBar` pills between breadcrumb and table
7. Update this `.agent` in the same session with **complete standalone context** (not terse notes): living sections + Change Log must fully brief the next agent — see `.cursor/rules/agent-context-completeness.mdc`.
8. Work is incomplete until code **and** `.agent` match, and a new chat could continue correctly from `.agent` alone.

## UI / UX Conventions (Mandatory)
- Visual language comes from existing admin theme (`theme.config.tsx`, Tailwind primary/secondary, `panel`, shared components) — do not invent a parallel look.
- List pages: compact tables with high-signal columns; wrap tables in overflow-x-auto; **`table-layout: auto`** (not fixed — fixed dumped leftover space into Title/Event and squeezed Capacity/Paid/Actions into `Capac...` / `P...` / `Actio...`). Give every column an explicit `width`; Actions min ~44px per icon. Cell text is `text-sm`, not `text-xs`.
- Status / type pills use `statusBadgeClass` (`bg-primary/10 text-primary`, Participant = `info`). **Never** theme `.badge` (that class forces `text-white` — Participant was invisible on white).
- Row-click to a full page must ignore clicks on `button` / `a` / `.btn`. Action icons `stopPropagation` so Edit/Delete do not open View.
- Datatable row actions (`utils/columns.ts` + `ActionType`): **`view`** (eye), **`edit`** (pencil), **`delete`** (trash), **`restore`**, **`permissions`**, **`status`** (UserCog — suspend/reactivate), **`archive`** (Archive box — package archive). Organizer list uses `status` for the status modal; Packages uses `archive` for archive. Do **not** reuse `edit` for status or `delete` for archive (same icon collision).
- Amount/currency cells: right-aligned, full `"15.00 USD"` via `formatMoney`, min width so they never clip.
- **Status filters:** `StatusFilterBar` (filled active pill) sits between breadcrumb and table on Events, Organizers, Users, Payments, Payouts, Certificates, Feedback, Subscriptions, QR Scan History. Extra pickers (dates, comboboxes) go in `extra`. Switching pills resets the table to page 1.
- **Side panel vs full page (data volume):**
  - Side panel (~8 fields, no nested lists): Users, Payments, Subscriptions, QR Scan History, Roles, Packages, Categories, Invitation templates, API clients, Logs.
  - Full page `pages/<resource>/show.tsx` + `/{resource}/:id` + back button + row-click: **Events** (tabbed hub), **Organizers**, **Payouts**, **Certificates**, **Feedback**.
- Event hub tabs (lazy, in order): Overview, Ticket Types, Registrations, Payments, Speakers, Sessions, Sponsors, Announcements, Form Fields, Gallery, Invitation, Analytics. `EventAddOnOversight` accepts `only` so unused add-on queries do not fire.
- **Event hub nested data is tables, not cards:** Ticket Types + Discount codes, Registrations, Payments (`StatusFilterBar` + table), Speakers/Sessions/Sponsors/Announcements, Form Fields, Gallery (thumbnail + file + remove). Overview stays fields + `EventMetricCard`. Invitation is a read-only preview: template thumbnail, `EventField` customizations with color swatches, overlay positions as `SimpleAdminTable` (Element / X / Y / Width / Height / Font size) — never dump `x=300, y=820` strings. Analytics uses `EventMetricCard` (not a table). Reuse `SimpleAdminTable` + `statusBadgeClass` + `formatMoney`.
- Forms/modals: shared `components/form/*` + `GenericModal`; CTAs use `btn btn-primary` patterns.
- Dense spacing in admin surfaces; avoid sparse “marketing” whitespace in sidebars/tables.
- New UI must include `dark:` variants consistent with neighboring screens.

## Update Protocol (Mandatory)

When any future chat changes code, this `.agent` file must be updated in the same work session.

### Completeness Bar (for other agents)
`.agent` must remain a **full project briefing**. After every update, another agent reading only this file must understand:
- how to run the app and current runtime state
- architecture and request flow
- mandatory backend/frontend/UI patterns
- current module inventory and exceptions
- what changed in this session (files, behavior, migrations/env, verification)

Do not write vague Change Log-only stubs. Sync living sections whenever reality changed.

### Minimum Required Updates Per Change
1. Update `Last updated` date + short summary.
2. Append a Change Log entry with:
   - date
   - short title
   - files touched
   - behavior change
   - migration/config/env impact
   - verification performed
3. If architecture/routes/modules/permissions/data model/UI conventions/runtime state changed, update the matching sections above (especially **Current Module Inventory** and scaffold/UI notes).
4. Self-check: could a new agent continue correctly from `.agent` alone? If not, expand until yes.

### Keep In Sync Rule
- If code and `.agent` disagree, `.agent` is stale and must be fixed immediately.
- No feature / refactor / bugfix is complete until `.agent` reflects the new state.

### Automated Enforcement
- Local pre-commit hook: `.git/hooks/pre-commit` runs `check-agent-update.sh`
- Guard script: `check-agent-update.sh`
- Installer: `install-agent-hook.ps1`
- CI gate: `.github/workflows/agent-context-check.yml`
- Rule: if staged/pushed changes touch critical project paths and `.agent` is not included, fail.

