### 2026-08-19 - Waafi HTTP 401 detection (real root cause)
- **Root cause confirmed from logs:** All real Waafi calls returned HTTP 401. Waafi 401 body is null, so `$response->json()` returned `[]`, and `extractFailureReason([])` correctly fell through to `"Payment was not approved."` — the extraction logic was fine, the underlying problem is missing/invalid credentials.
- Added temporary expanded diagnostic logging in `interpretResponse` (safe fields only), read logs, confirmed HTTP 401 with null body. Removed diagnostic logging afterward.
- Added HTTP 401 early-return in `interpretResponse`: `failure_code: gateway_auth_error`, `failure_reason: "Payment service configuration error. Please contact support."` — distinguishes a server-side config problem from a customer decline.
- Files: `WaafiPayService.php` (HTTP 401 path), `WaafiPayFailureMessageTest.php` (regression test `test_http_401_from_waafi_produces_gateway_auth_error`), `.agent`.
- Verification: 16 new tests passed; full suite **223 passed / 3 pre-existing ExceptionHandlerTest failures**.
- **Action required:** Configure valid Waafi credentials in `.env` (`WAAFI_MERCHANT_UID`, `WAAFI_API_USER_ID`, `WAAFI_API_KEY`) to resolve real payment failures.

### 2026-08-19 - Waafi failure-message extraction + participant payment API fix
- **Root cause:** `WaafiPayService::failureResult()` called `mapFailure($responseMsg)` which only looked at `responseMsg` and never read `params.description` from the Waafi body. When `responseMsg` was a technical code not in the static map, `failure_reason` became `"Payment failed: {technicalCode}"` or `"Payment failed."`. The participant API also returned the entire Eloquent model (serialized via `toArray()`) which does expose `failure_reason` on the model — so for known codes it would have worked, but the extraction didn't surface the actual Waafi human message.
- **Fix:** Added `extractFailureReason(array $body)`, `resolveFailureCode(?string)`, `sanitizeCustomerMessage(string)` to `WaafiPayService`. `failureResult()` now uses `extractFailureReason` with the full response body. `ParticipantPaymentController` now returns an explicit `serializePayment()` array with `failure_code` + `failure_reason` always present.
- Files: `WaafiPayService.php`, `ParticipantPaymentController.php`, `WaafiPayFailureMessageTest.php`, `.agent`.
- Verification: 15 new tests passed; full suite **222 passed / 3 pre-existing ExceptionHandlerTest failures**.

### 2026-08-19 - Participant auth: reset-code expiry + mail setting lookup
- **Password reset expiry:** migration `2026_08_19_100000_add_reset_code_expires_at_to_users_table.php` adds nullable `users.reset_code_expires_at`. `POST /auth/forgot-password` sets `reset_code_expires_at = now()->addMinutes(30)`. `POST /auth/reset-password` rejects expired codes (400, stable message); success clears code + expiry and revokes all User tokens (unchanged).
- **Mail setting consistency:** `SettingsSeeder` now seeds canonical `name=smtp` / `slug=email-smtp` (inactive, no credentials). `Settings::EMAIL_SMTP_NAME` + `scopeEmailSmtp()` (case-insensitive lookup) used by `MailService`, `SettingsController`. Architecture unchanged: queued mail still reads active DB SMTP, not `MAIL_MAILER=log`.
- Files: `AuthController.php`, `User.php`, `Settings.php`, `MailService.php`, `SettingsController.php`, `SettingsSeeder.php`, migration, `ParticipantPasswordResetTest.php`, `MailSettingsLookupTest.php`, `.agent`.
- Verification: `php artisan test --filter=ParticipantPasswordResetTest` (6 passed), `MailSettingsLookupTest` (2 passed); full `composer test` — **207 passed / 3 pre-existing `ExceptionHandlerTest` failures**.

